        "text": "Lilian Jimenez is an attorney who has focused on labor and immigration policy. She was first elected to the Illinois House in November 2022. She chairs the House Housing Committee. Her campaign says she was chief sponsor of the Safe Schools Act to protect K-12 students from immigration enforcement, and sponsored HB 1312, which allows residents to sue federal agents for constitutional violations. Her campaign says she supports taxing corporations and the wealthy to invest in healthcare, housing and education. It also says she wants to stabilize property taxes so longtime residents can remain in their neighborhoods. She passed a resolution honoring Arise Chicago for its workers' rights advocacy and a bill changing the will depository process.",
